e,v=ev(72,'31–39','Kṛtavīrya says many births’ merit now bears fruit in seeing Dattātreya and predicts future good from his favour, since wrongdoers do not see such sages. Dattātreya explicitly says he came to see the king’s extraordinary son. The king again laments his apparently fruitless practices and describes the son as a thorn in his heart. He brings the boy; the sage covers his eyes, then knows the relevant action through meditation. He predicts this very son will conquer all and diagnoses the king’s failure to perform ācamana after yawning during the Sankaṣṭa vigil as dishonouring the distress-removing vow. The son was born without limbs but can become complete through a remedy. The king accepts the diagnosis and asks what method will restore his son through the sage’s favour.',[(KV,F),(DT,S),(SON,F),('Gaṇeśa',D)],story=S1,outcome='Meditative diagnosis identifies one exact ritual omission; the father asks a remedy, without a new unnamed sin being invented.')
val(KV,'attributed_ritual_diagnosis','Dattātreya diagnoses omitted ācamana after yawning during Sankaṣṭa-vow vigil72.38 as causing the limb-deficient birth; king accepts and asks remedy39.',e)
val(KV,'request_to_dattatreya','A method through the sage’s favour by which his son becomes complete in limbs72.39.',e)
e,v=ev(72,'40–43','Compassionate Dattātreya teaches the CHILD the one-syllable mantra with its auxiliaries and prescribes devotional Gaṇeśa worship with it, fasting and one-meal rules. He predicts that after twelve years Gaṇeśa will give the child sight of himself and the deity’s mere glance will produce a divine body. Taking leave of the king, the sage disappears.',[(DT,S),(SON,F),(KV,F),('Gaṇeśa',D),('Single-syllable Gaṇeśa mantra',T)],story=S1,outcome='Actual guru instruction is distinguished from the future appearance-and-glance prediction.')
rel(DT,'teaches_mantra_to',SON,e);rel(SON,'receives_guru_instruction_from',DT,e,'GURU')
p_instr=power(SON,e,v,grant=DT,worshipped_id=names['Gaṇeśa'],granted='One-syllable mantra with auxiliaries is taught to the child.',mechanism='Prescribed fasting/one-meal worship; predicts Gaṇeśa appearance after twelve years and divine body through his mere glance.',notes='The glance is a guru’s future prediction, not the subsequently narrated actual transformation mechanism. Twelve years describes required practice/predicted appearance, not the boon’s lasting duration.')
e,v=ev(72,'44–47','After Dattātreya leaves, the footless son asks Kṛtavīrya to take him to a deep forest so he can practice for Gaṇeśa’s favour. Both parents weep at his request. The father sends him to a fine forest in a human-carried conveyance; servants place him in a leaf hut and return to the city. The boy remains there, firmly resolved on tapas.',[(SON,F),(KV,F),(Q,F),('Kārtavīrya forest human-carried conveyance','VAHANA'),('Kārtavīrya forest servants','FAMILY'),('Kārtavīrya tapas leaf hut',L),('Gaṇeśa',D)],story=S1,outcome='Actual relocation with servants and a leaf hut prepares the child’s separate twelve-year practice.')
rel(SON,'performs_tapas_at','Kārtavīrya tapas leaf hut',e)
e,v=ev(73,'1–6','The boy regularly japs the guru’s mantra, meditates Gaṇeśa with firm dedication, and lives on air without food like earth-clod or stone. Twelve years pass. Verse3 describes his condition with the printed nirvāṇam, retained without interpreting it as death or selecting another precise state. Pleased by his dedication and devotion, coral-formed Gaṇeśa rises from the pond and faces him. He notes the twelve years in the deserted forest frequented by lions and tigers and offers a boon according to the boy’s wish. Hearing him, the boy resumes bodily awareness.',[(SON,F),(DT,S),('Gaṇeśa',D),('Coral Gaṇeśa appearance in73','MANIFESTATION'),('Kārtavīrya tapas pond in73',L)],story=S1,outcome='Twelve-year air-fed practice leads to an actual coral-form appearance and boon invitation; the exact nirvāṇam condition remains under review.')
rel('Coral Gaṇeśa appearance in73','manifestation_of','Gaṇeśa',e)
e,v=ev(73,'7–9','The explicitly named son of Kṛtavīrya bows and speaks before many sages in vimānas. He requests continual nondeviating devotion to the deity’s feet, saying he has no enthusiasm to ask anything else. Nevertheless, to satisfy his parents, he also asks beauty of body pleasing to all.',[(SON,F),(KV,F),('Gaṇeśa',D),('Witnessing sages in73','FAMILY')],story=S1,outcome='The two requested benefits and the parents’ happiness motive are explicit; no demand for a thousand arms is put in the child’s mouth.')
req_e=e;req_ev=v
p=power(SON,e,v,typ='BOON',grant='Gaṇeśa',worshipped_id=names['Gaṇeśa'],motive='Please his parents through bodily beauty.',requested='Continual nondeviating devotion; additionally bodily beauty pleasing to all for his parents’ happiness.',notes='Personal boon invitation and requests. Subsequent physical response will be separately evidenced; no explicit verbal assent to the devotion request is supplied.')
p_body=p
e,v=ev(73,'10–15','Hearing the requests, māyā-bearing Gaṇeśa adopts aṇimā and enters the boy’s belly. With this entry Kṛtavīrya’s son gains a divine body with one thousand arms and two straight legs, standing like a mountain. Gods and divine sages shower flowers and praise both boy and deity with music. Kārtavīrya roars thunderously; the figure called Samavartin is greatly frightened and all earthly kings tremble, anticipating that he could shoot five hundred arrows in combat.',[(SON,F),(KV,F),('Gaṇeśa',D),('Coral Gaṇeśa appearance in73','MANIFESTATION'),('Gods',C),('Divine sages','FAMILY'),('Samavartin in73 fear reference','EPITHET'),('Kings witnessing Kārtavīrya in73','FAMILY')],story=S1,outcome='Actual aṇimā entry restores a divine thousand-armed/two-legged body. Five hundred combat arrows are an anticipated capacity, not an enacted battle.')
p_body['granted']='Actual divine body with one thousand arms and two straight legs.';p_body['mechanism']='Gaṇeśa adopts aṇimā and enters the boy’s belly.';p_body['evidence_ids'].append(e);p_body['field_evidence']['granted']=[e];p_body['field_evidence']['mechanism']=[e];p_body['later_event_ids'].append(v)
p_instr['later_event_ids'].append(v);p_instr['notes']+=' Actual73.10–12 uses aṇimā entry rather than explicitly enacting the predicted glance.';p_instr['evidence_ids'].append(e)
val(SON,'source_body_after_transformation','Divine body, one thousand arms and two straight legs73.10–12.',e)
power(SON,e,v,mechanism='Kings anticipate his capacity to release five hundred arrows in combat.',notes='Anticipated capacity73.15, not a narrated volley or invented weapon-counter sequence.')
e,v=ev(73,'16–19','Brahmā and the other deities descend from their vimānas and give the boy varied boons. They say deities will regain lost objects through remembrance of him; he will remove the heart-resident ā maya of all worlds. They call him an actual Viṣṇu form with the name Sahasrārjuna, promise fame in three worlds for a kalpa, protection of good people and those taking refuge, victory over all enemies and sovereignty of the earth. The deity group then disappears.',[(SON,F),('Brahmā',D),('Brahmā-led deity boon group in73','FAMILY'),('Gods',C),('Viṣṇu',D),('Sahasrārjuna name in73','EPITHET')],story=S1,outcome='These later grants have a collective divine grantor; they are separated from Gaṇeśa’s earlier physical response.')
rel('Sahasrārjuna name in73','source_name_of',SON,e);val(SON,'attributed_divine_identity','The Brahmā-led group calls him an actual Viṣṇu form73.17; source boon speech attribution.',e)
power(SON,e,v,typ='BOON',grant='Brahmā-led deity boon group in73',granted='Deities’ recovery of lost objects through remembrance of him; removal of all worlds’ heart-resident ā maya; Viṣṇu-form/Sahasrārjuna designation; three-world fame for a kalpa; good/refugee protection; victory over all enemies and earth sovereignty.',duration='A kalpa qualifies his three-world fame73.18.',notes='No exact request to this deity group is narrated. Āmaya is retained as heart-resident affliction, not a specific modern cardiac diagnosis. Remembrance/lost objects is not broadened beyond the verse’s deity wording.')
e,v=ev(73,'20–22','All kings bring elephants, horses, human conveyances, parasols, fly-whisks, lamps, chariots and other gifts. With Brahmins leading, Kārtavīrya installs a coral Gaṇeśa image in a great temple. Brahmins name it Pravālagaṇapa. He gives villages to the Brahmins appointed for its worship.',[(SON,F),('Kings witnessing Kārtavīrya in73','FAMILY'),('Pravālagaṇapa coral image',C),('Pravāla Gaṇeśa temple in73',L),('Pravālagaṇapa worship Brahmins','FAMILY'),('Gaṇeśa',D)],story=S1,outcome='An actual installed coral image and endowed worship establish the site after the transformation.')
rel('Pravālagaṇapa coral image','installed_at','Pravāla Gaṇeśa temple in73',e)
S2='gup6-story-sesa-pravala'
e,v=ev(73,'23–26','The place becomes famous as wish-accomplishing Pravāla-kṣetra. In a separate earlier account Śeṣa practices there desiring to bear earth and obtains many boons from Gaṇeśa: earth-bearing strength, omniscience, one thousand heads and supremacy among nine Nāga clans. With delighted mind he earlier installs the deity, bringing the second name Dharaṇīdhara, granting all wished fruits to those who remember or hear it.',[('Śeṣa',D),('Gaṇeśa',D),('Pravāla-kṣetra / Dharaṇīdhara site',L),('Dharaṇīdhara image installed by Śeṣa',C),('Nine Nāga clans in73','FAMILY'),('Dharaṇīdhara remembrance/hearing beneficiaries','FAMILY')],story=S2,outcome='A source flashback explains the second site-name; Śeṣa’s boons are not assigned to Kārtavīrya.')
rel('Dharaṇīdhara image installed by Śeṣa','installed_by','Śeṣa',e);rel('Dharaṇīdhara image installed by Śeṣa','installed_at','Pravāla-kṣetra / Dharaṇīdhara site',e)
power('Śeṣa',e,v,typ='BOON',grant='Gaṇeśa',motive='Bear earth.',austerity_or_circumstances='Earlier observance at this site.',granted='Earth-bearing capacity, omniscience, one thousand heads, supremacy among nine Nāga clans.',notes='Motive explicitly stated; the wording of a personal request is not given. Chronology is an embedded earlier practice/installation.')
power('Dharaṇīdhara remembrance/hearing beneficiaries',e,v,mechanism='All desired fruits.',trigger='Remember or hear the Dharaṇīdhara name/account73.26.',notes='The precise formula speaks of remembering/hearing, without inventing a visit or separate practice requirement.')
e,v=ev(73,'27–28','Sahasrabāhu honours the Brahmins and takes leave of the kings, then returns to his city to see his mother and father. Both parents and the city rejoice at his restored form. His parents give varied gifts to eminent Brahmins.',[(SON,F),(KV,F),(Q,F),('Pravālagaṇapa worship Brahmins','FAMILY'),('Kings witnessing Kārtavīrya in73','FAMILY'),('Kṛtavīrya assembled public','FAMILY')],story=S1,outcome='The son actually returns to both parents and receives their joy; the birth/remedy/reunion sequence has a bounded ending.')
S3='gup6-story-surasena-merit-frame'
e,v=ev(73,'29–36','Indra closes the Sankaṣṭa glory, saying it became known in the mortal world through Kṛtavīrya’s son and was experienced by gods and kings such as Candraseṇa. Remembrance alone gives accomplishment. Briefly, Rāvaṇa received the printed akhilājñatā and the Pāṇḍavas obtained their kingdom through its favour. Indra says his stalled vimāna will move to Amarāvatī if this vow’s merit is given into his hand. Brahmā says Śūrasena hears joyfully, bows to Indra, praises his own earlier merit for hearing such a vow and begins practicing. No merit transfer or actual departure occurs here.',[('Indra',D),('Brahmā',D),('Śūrasena',F),(SON,F),('Candraseṇa',F),('Rāvaṇa',A),('Pāṇḍavas',C),('Indra stalled vimāna','VAHANA'),('Amarāvatī',L),('Sankaṣṭa-caturthī practitioners','FAMILY')],story=S3,outcome='The exemplum returns to the stalled-vimāna frame with a conditional merit request; Śūrasena starts a vow, while the vehicle remains unresolved.')
power('Sankaṣṭa-caturthī practitioners',e,v,mechanism='Accomplishment even through remembering the vow73.30.',trigger='Remember Sankaṣṭa-caturthī.')
power('Pāṇḍavas',e,v,mechanism='Reported earlier attainment of their kingdom through the vow’s favour.',notes='Only the brief reported result73.31 is extracted; no epic battle or genealogy is added.')
power('Rāvaṇa',e,v,granted='Printed akhilājñatā73.31, exact interpretation pending.',notes='The source’s terse efficacy claim is retained raw; no silent omniscience or other translated benefit.',verification_status='NEEDS_REVIEW')
u=note_evidence(73,'3,31','73.3 prints nirvāṇaṃ tasya before the living child’s boon encounter; its precise condition is not normalized to death.73.31 prints akhilājñatā for Rāvaṇa’s brief vow-result; an exact English benefit is withheld.','NEEDS_REVIEW')
variant('73-lexical-benefits','Exact nirvāṇam condition and Rāvaṇa akhilājñatā need grammatical or edition support. Actual physical response/reunion and the named Śeṣa boons remain independently readable.',u)
